  rankdir="TB";
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study proposes to investigate how selective perturbation, including inhibition or depletion assays, of host-cell homologous-recombination and non-homologous end-joining DNA-repair factors affects rAAV vector genome concatenation and gene expression, with the goal of identifying pathway controls that can improve the efficiency and effective payload size of dual-vector recombinant AAV gene therapies.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When dual-vector rAAV therapies are constrained by payload capacity, inefficient or random genome joining, and incomplete mechanistic knowledge of host DNA-repair control, the appropriate research proposal is to experimentally map and selectively perturb candidate host-cell DNA-repair pathways to identify which activities promote concatenation and expression."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Together, rAAV capsid payload limits, promoter-control problems, host-factor orchestration of nuclear transduction steps, NHEJ involvement in vector genome concatenation, host-factor plausibility for circularization and concatenation, dual-vector efficiency limits, and HR-mediated split-gene reconstitution motivate studying host-cell DNA-repair control of rAAV vector genome concatenation and expression in dual-vector gene therapy."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Because ITR-ITR joining is analogous to host DNA repair mechanisms and double-stranded rAAV vector genomes could resemble chromosomal breaks, host cellular factors are plausible mediators of rAAV vector genome circularization and concatenation."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) Random ITR joining in dual-vector rAAV systems and reliance on very high vector doses support the conclusion that current dual-vector approaches have efficiency limitations and incompletely understood mechanisms."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) The highly recombinogenic alkaline phosphatase fragment supports the hypothesis that homologous recombination can promote annealing of opposite-sense rAAV vector genomes and reconstitution of a larger split gene in a dual-vector context."];
  "n1" [label="(4,0,0) Currently there is The unenveloped 25 nm capsid can package no more than 5 kb of ssDNA into its small lumen."];
